**What I changed (real engineering writes in the project, not scratch):**

1. **`src/contract.rs`** — promoted the player's velocity from the private struct in `game.rs` into the registered contract as `hof_game::contract::Velocity { x, y }` (`#[reflect(Component)]` + `register_type`), so a movement failure can be localised on the wire (`InputIntent.move_dir = 1` with `Velocity.x = 0` is a plumbing bug; non-zero `Velocity.x` with frozen `Transform.translation.x` is an integration bug). All seven frozen surfaces plus `ProcessNonce` remain declared and registered under their original paths.

2. **`src/game.rs`** — implemented and hardened the five PRD behaviours on the frozen surfaces:
   - `count_frames` increments `FrameCounter.frames` exactly once per frame (D297 (b));
   - `apply_input` derives `Velocity.x` *from scratch* every frame from the level-triggered `InputIntent.move_dir` (so `0` stops the player with no residual velocity) and consumes the jump's edge via a private `JumpLatch` (one press = one jump);
   - `integrate` applies `JUMP_SPEED = 300` / `GRAVITY = 1200` (≈0.5 s air time, ~30 frames — an arc the battery can sample in both directions), clamps at `GROUND_Y`, and keeps `Grounded.on_ground` true while standing / false while airborne;
   - `collect_coin_and_win` latches `CoinCounter.coins` 0→1 at `COIN_X = 60` and `WinFlag.won` false→true at `GOAL_X = 100`, both one-way and both walkable on the same ground plane;
   - the frame pipeline is `count_frames → apply_input → integrate → collect_coin_and_win` (chained), and the per-frame maths was factored into three small helpers so it is testable without a clock.

**Verified locally:** `cargo build --offline` exits 0 with no warnings; `cargo test --offline` passes 6/6 unit tests driving the exact same helpers (held input moves 100 px in 30 frames and release freezes x with `velocity.x == 0`; the jump rises then falls and lands with `Grounded` true again; a held press yields exactly one take-off; coin 0→1 and win false→true are reached by walking right and survive walking back left). I did not start a game or touch the battery; the runtime's session and the Tester judge the running artifact.

